From 21b4de4f13c852107a620ef263a8feed6f8032bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Xiwen <forbidden405@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Apr 2023 13:59:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] dt-bindings: clock: split histb-clock into two headers

The CRG driver of each SoC provides different clocks and resets, so one
generic header across all HiSTB SoCs is wrong. Split histb-clock.h into
hisilicon,hi3798cv200-crg.h and hisilicon,hi3798cv200-sysctrl.h and keep
histb-clock.h as a deprecated wrapper that includes both for backward
compatibility only.

Acked-by: Krzysztof Kozlowski <krzysztof.kozlowski@linaro.org>
Signed-off-by: Yang Xiwen <forbidden405@outlook.com>
Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
